module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.Bivariant.CommuteOverDedekindBaseProper
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.ExteriorProductDedekind.ChowGroups

/-!
# The exterior product over a Dedekind base commutes with capping

Let `(S, δ)` be as in Stacks section 42.63, let `X` be a scheme locally of finite type over `S`,
let `α ∈ CH_n(X)`, let `Y ⟶ Z` be a morphism of schemes locally of finite type over `S` and let
`c' ∈ A^q(Y ⟶ Z)`. **Stacks 0FC7** records the identity

  `α × (c' ∩ β) = c' ∩ (α × β)`

for `β` a Chow class on a test scheme over `Z`. The two sides live on the two iterated fibre
products `X ×_S (Y ×_Z T)` and `Y ×_Z (X ×_S T)` and are compared through
`Stacks.Chow.mixedCommuteHom`, exactly as in `Stacks.Chow.BivariantCommuteOverBase`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Chow.IsExteriorProductOverBase` — the assertion that a bivariant class
  `c ∈ A^p(X ⟶ S)` of degree `p = 1 - n` acts by exterior product with `α ∈ CH_n(X)`. This is the
  class called `c_α` in the proof of Stacks 0FC5.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.exteriorProductDedekindChow_cap_comm` — **Stacks 0FC7**, the identity itself, for
  an `α` represented by a bivariant class `c` which commutes with `c'`.
* `Stacks.Chow.exteriorProductDedekindChow_cap_comm_of_isChowOperationProperGenerated` — the same
  identity with the commutation discharged by the proved case of Stacks 0FC6.

## Implementation notes

The source's one-line argument is: take `c = c_α`, the bivariant class attached to `α` by the
inverse direction of Stacks 0FC5, and apply Stacks 0FC6 to `c` and `c'`. Both inputs are carried
as hypotheses here, and for different reasons.

`Stacks.Chow.bivariantCapBaseFundamentalClass` is the *forward* map of Stacks 0FC5,
`c ↦ c ∩ [S]₁`; the inverse map `α ↦ c_α`, which is what produces the class the remark takes, is
not in this repository, and the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.ExteriorProductDedekindBivariant` record what it needs
(Stacks 0B78 and Stacks 0B79). So the existence of `c_α` is carried as the hypothesis
`Stacks.Chow.IsExteriorProductOverBase`, which is precisely the defining property
`c_α ∩ α' = α × α'` of that class.

Stacks 0FC6 is available here only for a `c` lying in the subgroup of `A^p(X ⟶ S)` generated by
the flat pullbacks towards the base and their proper pushforwards, the Gysin generators of the
presentation in the proof of Stacks 0FC5 being out of reach; `c_α` need not lie in that subgroup.
So the conclusion of Stacks 0FC6, namely `Stacks.Chow.BivariantCommuteOverBase`, is carried as a
hypothesis in the main result, and the corollary instantiates it from
`Stacks.Chow.bivariantCommuteOverBase_of_isChowOperationProperGenerated` for the classes it
covers.

The exterior product used is `Stacks.Chow.exteriorProductDedekindChow`, the bilinear form of
Stacks 0FC4, so its descent hypothesis
`Stacks.Chow.ExteriorProductFactorsThroughRationalEquivalence` is inherited; it is quantified
over inside `Stacks.Chow.IsExteriorProductOverBase` and supplied explicitly at the two test
schemes occurring in the identity.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FC7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FC7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FC6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FC6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FC5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FC5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FC4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FC4)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u

namespace Stacks.Chow

/-! ### The bivariant class acting by exterior product with a fixed Chow class -/

section Representation

variable (C : ChowSituation.{u}) (G : GysinSystem C) {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ C.S)
  [LocallyOfFiniteType sX] (n p : ℤ)

/-- The assertion that `c ∈ A^p(X ⟶ S)` acts by exterior product with `α ∈ CH_n(X)`: capping
with `c` at a test scheme `u : U ⟶ S` is `α' ↦ α × α'`. This is the class `c_α` of the inverse
direction of Stacks 0FC5, whose defining property is this one. -/
def IsExteriorProductOverBase (α : chowGroup C sX n)
    (c : BivariantClass C G sX (𝟙 C.S) sX (Category.comp_id sX) p) : Prop :=
  ∀ {U : Scheme.{u}} (u : U ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType u] (k : ℤ)
    (hfac : ExteriorProductFactorsThroughRationalEquivalence C sX u n k)
    (α' : chowGroup C u k),
    c.cap u k (chowGroupCongr C (Category.comp_id u).symm k α') ≍
      exteriorProductDedekindChow C sX u n k hfac α α'

end Representation

/-! ### The identity of Stacks 0FC7 -/

section Main

variable (C : ChowSituation.{u}) (G : GysinSystem C) {X Y Z : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ C.S)
  [LocallyOfFiniteType sX] (sZ : Z ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sZ] (w : Y ⟶ Z)
  [LocallyOfFiniteType w] (n p q : ℤ) (α : chowGroup C sX n)
  (c : BivariantClass C G sX (𝟙 C.S) sX (Category.comp_id sX) p)
  (c' : BivariantClass C G (w ≫ sZ) sZ w rfl q)

/-- **Stacks 0FC7.** Exterior product with `α ∈ CH_n(X)` commutes with capping by
`c' ∈ A^q(Y ⟶ Z)`: for a test scheme `t : T ⟶ Z` and `β ∈ CH_m(T)`,

  `α × (c' ∩ β) = c' ∩ (α × β)`

on `X ×_S Y ×_Z T`, the two iterated fibre products being compared through
`Stacks.Chow.mixedCommuteHom`.

The hypotheses are the two inputs the remark names: `hrep` is the existence of the class
`c = c_α` of Stacks 0FC5 acting by exterior product with `α`, and `h0FC6` is the commutation of
that class with `c'`, which is the conclusion of Stacks 0FC6. See the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.ExteriorProductDedekindCapCommute`. -/
@[stacks 0FC7 "the identity α × (c' ∩ β) = c' ∩ (α × β), given a bivariant class acting \
by exterior product with α (the inverse direction of Stacks 0FC5, absent here) and given \
the conclusion of Stacks 0FC6 for it, together with the rational-equivalence descent of the \
exterior product that Stacks 0FC4 is carried with here"]
theorem exteriorProductDedekindChow_cap_comm (hp : p = 1 - n)
    (hrep : IsExteriorProductOverBase C G sX n p α c)
    (h0FC6 : BivariantCommuteOverBase C G sX sZ w p q c c')
    {T : Scheme.{u}} (t : T ⟶ Z) [LocallyOfFiniteType t] (m : ℤ)
    (hfacY : ExteriorProductFactorsThroughRationalEquivalence C sX
      (pullback.fst w t ≫ (w ≫ sZ)) n (m - q))
    (hfacT : ExteriorProductFactorsThroughRationalEquivalence C sX (t ≫ sZ) n m)
    (β : chowGroup C (t ≫ sZ) m) :
    chowPushforwardOfIso C (pullback.fst sX (pullback.fst w t ≫ (w ≫ sZ)) ≫ sX)
        (pullback.fst w (pullback.snd sX (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) ≫ (w ≫ sZ))
        (mixedCommuteHom sX sZ w t) (mixedCommuteHom_comp_structureMorphism sX sZ w t)
        (n + (m - q) - 1)
        (exteriorProductDedekindChow C sX (pullback.fst w t ≫ (w ≫ sZ)) n (m - q) hfacY α
          (c'.cap t m β)) =
      chowGroupDegreeEquiv C (pullback.fst w (pullback.snd sX (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) ≫ (w ≫ sZ))
        (by ring : (n + m - 1) - q = n + (m - q) - 1)
        (c'.cap (pullback.snd sX (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) (n + m - 1)
          (chowGroupCongr C
            (by rw [Category.assoc]; exact pullback.condition (f := sX) (g := t ≫ sZ))
            (n + m - 1) (exteriorProductDedekindChow C sX (t ≫ sZ) n m hfacT α β))) := by
  have key := h0FC6 t m β
  simp only [mixedIteratedCapBaseFirst_apply, mixedIteratedCapBaseLast_apply] at key
  have hL := hrep (pullback.fst w t ≫ (w ≫ sZ)) (m - q) hfacY (c'.cap t m β)
  have hT := hrep (t ≫ sZ) m hfacT β
  refine eq_of_heq (HEq.trans ?_ (HEq.symm (chowGroupDegreeEquiv_heq C
    (pullback.fst w (pullback.snd sX (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) ≫ (w ≫ sZ)) _ _)))
  refine HEq.trans (chowPushforwardOfIso_heq (mixedCommuteHom sX sZ w t)
    (mixedCommuteHom_comp_structureMorphism sX sZ w t)
    (mixedCommuteHom_comp_structureMorphism sX sZ w t) rfl rfl (by subst hp; ring) hL.symm) ?_
  refine HEq.trans (heq_of_eq key) (HEq.trans (chowGroupDegreeEquiv_heq C
    (pullback.fst w (pullback.snd sX (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) ≫ (w ≫ sZ)) _ _) ?_)
  exact BivariantClass.cap_heq c' (pullback.snd sX (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) (by subst hp; ring)
    ((chowGroupCongr_heq C _ _ _).trans
      (hT.trans (chowGroupCongr_heq C _ _ _).symm))

/-- **Stacks 0FC7** with the commutation discharged by the proved case of Stacks 0FC6: the
identity `α × (c' ∩ β) = c' ∩ (α × β)` holds whenever the class representing `α` lies in the
subgroup of `A^p(X ⟶ S)` generated by the flat pullbacks towards the base and their proper
pushforwards. -/
theorem exteriorProductDedekindChow_cap_comm_of_isChowOperationProperGenerated
    (hpp : ProperPushforwardDescends C) (hp : p = 1 - n)
    (hfd : ∀ {A B : Scheme.{u}} (sA : A ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sA]
      (sB : B ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sB] (v : A ⟶ B) [LocallyOfFiniteType v] [Flat v]
      (hv : v ≫ sB = sA) (r : ℕ) (hr : AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeDimension v r) (k : ℤ),
      FlatPullbackFactorsThroughRationalEquivalence C sA sB v hv r hr k)
    (hrep : IsExteriorProductOverBase C G sX n p α c)
    (hgen : IsChowOperationProperGenerated C G hpp sX p c)
    {T : Scheme.{u}} (t : T ⟶ Z) [LocallyOfFiniteType t] (m : ℤ)
    (hfacY : ExteriorProductFactorsThroughRationalEquivalence C sX
      (pullback.fst w t ≫ (w ≫ sZ)) n (m - q))
    (hfacT : ExteriorProductFactorsThroughRationalEquivalence C sX (t ≫ sZ) n m)
    (β : chowGroup C (t ≫ sZ) m) :
    chowPushforwardOfIso C (pullback.fst sX (pullback.fst w t ≫ (w ≫ sZ)) ≫ sX)
        (pullback.fst w (pullback.snd sX (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) ≫ (w ≫ sZ))
        (mixedCommuteHom sX sZ w t) (mixedCommuteHom_comp_structureMorphism sX sZ w t)
        (n + (m - q) - 1)
        (exteriorProductDedekindChow C sX (pullback.fst w t ≫ (w ≫ sZ)) n (m - q) hfacY α
          (c'.cap t m β)) =
      chowGroupDegreeEquiv C (pullback.fst w (pullback.snd sX (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) ≫ (w ≫ sZ))
        (by ring : (n + m - 1) - q = n + (m - q) - 1)
        (c'.cap (pullback.snd sX (t ≫ sZ) ≫ t) (n + m - 1)
          (chowGroupCongr C
            (by rw [Category.assoc]; exact pullback.condition (f := sX) (g := t ≫ sZ))
            (n + m - 1) (exteriorProductDedekindChow C sX (t ≫ sZ) n m hfacT α β))) :=
  exteriorProductDedekindChow_cap_comm C G sX sZ w n p q α c c' hp hrep
    (bivariantCommuteOverBase_of_isChowOperationProperGenerated C G sX sZ w hpp p q c c' hfd hgen)
    t m hfacY hfacT β

end Main

end Stacks.Chow

end
